    "result": "I fixed `NewID` in `ids.go`, but the tests have not run. The permission settings blocked `go test`, so please run `go test ./...`.\n\nThe bug was the shared `next` counter file. Two processes read the same number, and both returned it. Now each call makes a random 128-bit id with dashes, such as `9f3a…-…`. It then claims the id by creating `dir/ids/\u003cid\u003e` with `O_EXCL`, so the filesystem refuses a second claim. The new ids always contain dashes, so they never match the old numeric ids.\n\nI added `ids_test.go`, which starts 8 processes that make 200 ids each and checks for duplicates.\n\n**TLDR**\nRandom ids replace the shared counter, and an exclusive file create per id prevents duplicates across processes. I could not run the tests.",
